  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "The length and width of a rectangle each increase by $20\\%$. By what percentage does the area increase?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$44\\%$.",
      "worked": "Let the original dimensions be $l$ and $w$, so the original area is $A=lw$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{new}}&=(1.2l)(1.2w)\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=1.44lw\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=1.44A.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe new area is $144\\%$ of the original area, so the increase is $44\\%$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
